            <ArticleTitle>[Role of xenobiotic biotransformation enzymes in susceptibility to bronchial asthma and in formation of its clinical phenotypic features].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>36-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The paper shows the impact of some mutations of CYP1A, GSTM1, GSTT1, and NAT2 genes and different combinations of alleles of these genes on susceptibility to bronchial asthma and its clinical features. Passive smoking modulates these relationships.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
